artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider the third-order rational difference equation
  z_{n+1} = (γ + α z_{n-1} + δ z_n z_{n-1} + α₁ β z_{n-1} z_{n-2}) / (C + A z_{n-1} + D z_n z_{n-1} + α₁ B z_{n-1} z_{n-2}),  n = 0, 1, 2, …,
where all parameters α, β, γ, δ, A, B, C, D, α₁ are nonnegative real numbers, and the initial conditions z_{-2}, z_{-1}, z_0 are nonnegative reals chosen so that every denominator that appears in the recursion is strictly positive. By restricting to subsets of the parameters that are allowed to vanish (and otherwise normalizing nonzero parameters to 1), one obtains a family of 225 distinct special cases of this equation. For each of these 225 special cases, determine:
  (i) the boundedness character of all admissible solutions (i.e., for which choices of nonnegative parameters and admissible initial conditions every solution is bounded, and for which choices unbounded solutions exist);
  (ii) the periodic character of solutions (existence, structure, and possible periods of periodic solutions, and convergence of solutions to such periodic cycles);
  (iii) the global stability character of every nonnegative equilibrium point (local stability, instability, and the global attractivity basin of each equilibrium).

